      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Any serious analyst understands that the market is pricing in the transition, and clinging to fossil fuels for two decades is a deliberate, high-risk bet against established global policy. The case for staying in oil and gas is purely based on short-term inertia, not long-term viability. Objectively, the world is moving toward cleaner energy, making continued heavy investment in fossil fuels a structurally declining asset class.",
      "source": "target",
